{ 0x54430001U, "# Dead or Alive 3 (USA), title 54430001, version 1\012# Asked for by SamuraiLegion (2026-11-19): Time Attack always plays at difficulty Normal with fixed rounds, whatever\012# Options > Game Settings say. The game starts every fight with a switch on the mode (code at 0x6E250); Time Attack\012# (mode 3) writes fixed values there: difficulty 1, rounds to win 2 (single) or 1 (tag). The other modes read\012# Options > Game Settings (Difficulty at 0x484D78: 0 Easy .. 3 Very Hard; Match Point at 0x484DB6, an index into the\012# rounds table at 0x306530: 1 2 3 4 5).\012# Two short helpers go into unused padding between functions (0x11101, 0x118D2: never called, nothing points there).\012# Tested 2026-11-19 on PC xemu 0.8.139 (memory written through its debugger): Very Hard + Match Point 4 -> Time Attack\012# fight with difficulty 3 and 4 round marks a side.\012title 54430001\012version 0x00000001\012\012[ta-settings] Time Attack uses your Difficulty and Match Point\012# off until the player turns it on in Game Vault (game details > Game patches), which sends patches=ta-settings\012default off\012# helper: difficulty setting -> the fight's difficulty (keeps every register and flag)\0120x00011101: 90 90 90 90 90 90 90 90 90 90 90 90 90 -> 50 A0 78 4D 48 00 A2 24 9D 47 00 58 C3\012# helper: Match Point setting -> rounds to win, in DL\0120x000118D2: 90 90 90 90 90 90 90 90 90 90 90 90 90 90 -> 0F B6 15 B6 4D 48 00 8A 92 30 65 30 00 C3\012# Time Attack: difficulty from the setting instead of 1 (single and tag)\0120x0006E395: 88 0D 24 9D 47 00 -> E8 67 2D FA FF 90\012# Time Attack single: rounds to win from the setting instead of 2\0120x0006E3A2: 8A 15 31 65 30 00 -> E8 2B 35 FA FF 90\012\012[ta-tag-rounds] Tag Time Attack uses Match Point too (normally 1 round)\012default off\0120x000118D2: 90 90 90 90 90 90 90 90 90 90 90 90 90 90 -> 0F B6 15 B6 4D 48 00 8A 92 30 65 30 00 C3\0120x0006E419: 8A 15 30 65 30 00 -> E8 B4 34 FA FF 90\012" },
